SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Page updated: Maine Board of Overseers of the
  Bar — General News
DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
 ge directly to review the update.\n\nWhat changed (text excerpt):\nAdded:\
 n  + 8/24/2026\n  + In re: Elizabeth E. LaPierre\n  + Single Justice\n  + 
 Receiver Appointment [PDF]\n  + Order for Appointment of Receiver\n  + 8/2
 4/2026\n  + Board of Overseers of the Bar v. Elizabeth E. LaPierre\, of Po
 rtland\, Maine\n  + Single Justice\n  + Immediate Interim Suspension [PDF]
 \n  + Suspension\nRemoved:\n  - FY27 Annual Attorney Registration is Open\
 n  - Attorney license renewal and Guardian ad Litem license renewal may be
  completed in the MyBoardAccess portal from July 1 through August 31\, 202
 6 at 5:00 pm.\n  - Pursuant to M. Bar R. 4\,\n  - Registration documents a
 nd payments received after August 31st will be assessed a non-waivable lat
 e fee.\n  - We greatly appreciate your updated contact information\, proxy
 \, and IOLTA account listing\, and service email for court service and not
 ices.\n  - If your status has changed since last year:\n  - new law clerk\
 n  - clerkship ended or is ending soon\n  - retired seeking to be Inactive
 \n  - new judge\n  - no longer a judge\n  - active military or changing st
 atus\n  - seeking to become active again\n  - Before you register in the p
 ortal\, please contact\n  - execassistant@mebaroverseers.org\n  - to reque
 st a status change.\n  - Please note\, if you still owe a CLE late fee you
 r license renewal/registration cannot be approved until that is resolved.\
 n  - Registration is completed online on the\n  - MyBoardAccess\n  - by cl
 icking on the Renew Registration section of the Board's web portal. A conf
 irmation email will automatically be sent to you from\n[diff truncated]\nh
 ttps://www.mebaroverseers.org/
URL:https://www.mebaroverseers.org/
