DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
 ge directly to review the update.\n\nWhat changed (text excerpt):\nAdded:\
 n  + Home\n  + Helpful Links\n  + Commission Guidance\n  + Meetings & Minu
 tes\n  + Annual Reports\n  + Mediation Payments\n  + Consumer tools\n  + A
 ttorney Referral Listing\n  + Sexual Harassment Trainer Listing\n  + Media
 tion Handbook\n  + How Do I?\n  + Check the status of a Complaint\n  + Req
 uest an Accommodation\n  + Contact MHRC\n  + Emerging Issues\n  + Covid19 
 Issues\n  + Homeless Pilot Project\n  + Latest News\n  + The Commission co
 nducts operations both in person and via electronic means according to age
 ncy policies that apply to parties\, attorneys\, and the public.\n  + Plea
 se find our policies about how to file documents/pleadings electronically 
 and otherwise\n  + here\n  + and our policies about public meetings\n  + h
 ere\n  + . Please contact us at\n  + info@mhrc.maine.gov\n  + or\n  + 207-
 \n  + 624-6290\n  + with questions.\n  + August 24\, 2026\, MHRC meeting a
 genda (\n  + PDF\n  + ) (Live on\n  + YouTube\n  + )\n  + MHRC and MDOL\, 
 along with Clara Porter from Prevention\, Action\, Change\, and Peter Lowe
 \, Esq.\, from Brann & Isaacson\, present a\n  + joint training on sexual 
 harassment\n  + in the workplace. This training can be used by employers t
 o comply with the 26 M.R.S. Section 807 requirement to provide training to
  new employees. Please note that presenting this training alone\n  + does 
 not\n  + meet the training requirement for supervisory and managerial empl
 oyees. This video is ASL-interpreted.\n  + MHRC Guidance on HUD Change\n  
 + to Definition of Assistance Animal\n  + October 31\, 2025:\n  + An\n[dif
 f truncated]\nhttps://www1.maine.gov/mhrc/laws-guidance/changes
URL:https://www1.maine.gov/mhrc/laws-guidance/changes
